Native shading M2 (metal/src/main/resources/mcopt/shade/shade_post.metal): the bloom composite (an energy-conserving lerp
toward the blurred image with octave weights i^s and a fog-weighted extra, instead of an additive threshold) follows SE
Natural Bloom & Dirty Lens, Copyright (c) 2019 sonicether, MIT License
(https://github.com/sonicether/SE-Natural-Bloom-Dirty-Lens); the code is an original Metal implementation. The 13-tap
downsample / tent upsample pyramid follows Jimenez 2014 (public talk); the tone curve follows Lottes 2016 (public talk);
the integer hash is Chris Wellons' lowbias32 (public domain).

Native shading TAAU (metal/src/main/resources/mcopt/shade/taa.metal): the 5-tap Catmull-Rom history fetch
(taaCatmullRom) is adapted from Matt Pettineo (MJP), "Bicubic texture filtering with the Catmull-Rom spline in 9 / 5
taps" (https://gist.github.com/TheRealMJP/c83b8c0f46b63f3a88a5986f4fa982b1), MIT License, with the corner taps dropped
as in Jimenez, "Filmic SMAA" (SIGGRAPH 2016). The output resolution's upscale (shade_post.metal shade_upscale) uses the
same 5-tap Catmull-Rom (MJP's gist, MIT License). The rest of the resolve is original, after public techniques (Karis 2014,
Salvi 2016, Yang et al. 2020).

Native shading M3 volumetric clouds (metal/src/main/resources/mcopt/shade/clouds.metal): portions adapted from Photon
Shaders (https://github.com/sixthsurge/photon), commit 26c2906e, Copyright (c) 2025 Benjamin Stott ("sixthsurge"), MIT
License (full text: LICENSES/MIT-Photon.txt): the cumulus altitude shaping, the "powder" term, the cloud phase function
as a mix of forward and backward lobes, the octave loop of the multiple-scattering approximation, the aerial perspective
blend by the clouds' apparent distance, and the checkerboard + reprojected-history upscaling. The history's 5-tap
Catmull-Rom fetch (cloudCatmullRom) is the MJP gist named under TAAU above, MIT License. The rest of the file is original
(Apache-2.0).

Native shading volumetric light, air mode (metal/src/main/resources/mcopt/shade/vl.metal, vl_march): portions adapted from
Photon Shaders (https://github.com/sixthsurge/photon), commit 26c2906e, Copyright (c) 2025 Benjamin Stott ("sixthsurge"), MIT
License (full text: LICENSES/MIT-Photon.txt), include/fog/air_fog_vl.glsl: the approach (one march of the height-layered air
from the camera to the scene with the sun's shadow at every step and the per-step energy-conserving integral) and the forest
air's phase function (a forward and a backward Henyey-Greenstein lobe, 0.7 / 0.3 with g 0.5 / -0.2, summed over four octaves
of a multiple-scattering approximation). The shade grid (vl_shade_grid), the shadowed-difference output and the rest of the
file are original (Apache-2.0).
